    "message": "feat(mcp): add ix mcp subcommand exposing the code graph as MCP tools (#219)\n\nRuns a dual-era MCP stdio server (2026-07-28 stateless + 2025-06-18\ninitialize handshake) exposing seven read-only tools bound to\nmap/status/explain/trace/impact/search/rank and reusing --format llm.\nTool arguments are validated against per-tool JSON schemas and executed\nvia the F-010 execFile pattern (no shell, hard timeout, kill on\nnotifications/cancelled). Registered in oss.ts with a regression guard\nmirroring the F-009 discipline (89ca55e); no Pro stub can shadow it.\nThe remap write tool is intentionally absent — /__ix/remap does not\nexist on this base (added by the unmerged hardening PR).\n\n34 new tests: protocol/validation units, in-memory dual-era session,\nregistration guard, and a real-process stdio integration test.",
